# Declare the text encoding explicitly.
#
# Without this, Git guesses, and on a Windows workstation a file written as UTF-8
# can get committed as something else. That is how php-api/db/schema.sql ended
# up double-encoded: a UTF-8 em dash (E2 80 94) stored as the eight bytes
# c3 a2 e2 82 ac e2 80 9d, which renders as "├óΓé¼ΓÇ¥".
#
# It is almost always a TERMINAL problem, not a file problem: PowerShell decodes
# UTF-8 output as Windows-1252, so a correct em dash prints as "ΓÇö". If you see
# that, the file is fine; run `chcp 65001` or use a UTF-8 terminal.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never diffed, never transcoded.
*.webp binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.pdf  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.woff  binary
*.ico  binary